.TH SDL_GUIDToString 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GUIDToString \- Get an ASCII string representation for a given
.BR SDL_GUID .

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_guid.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_GUIDToString(SDL_GUID guid, char *pszGUID, int cbGUID);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I guid
the
.BR SDL_GUID
you wish to convert to string\[char46]
.TP
.I pszGUID
buffer in which to write the ASCII string\[char46]
.TP
.I cbGUID
the size of pszGUID, should be at least 33 bytes\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

